cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its methodology, please cite it as below. For
  any result computed from the public corpus, also cite dataset v1.0.0 (see
  references).
title: "Idéfix: propagation and coordination analysis for Telegram public channels"
abstract: >-
  A demonstrator that maps observable diffusion and coordination structure
  across public Telegram channels and produces a ranked, explainable and
  auditable examination queue for human analysts. It never judges whether a
  message is true, and it is not a validated manipulation detector.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Labarrère
    given-names: Mickaël
    alias: mlabarrere
repository-code: "https://github.com/mlabarrere/Idefix"
url: "https://github.com/mlabarrere/Idefix"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.4.1
date-released: 2026-10-26
keywords:
  - disinformation
  - telegram
  - coordinated-behaviour
  - graph-analysis
  - influence-operations
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Idéfix Telegram public corpus (idefix-telegram-public-corpus)"
    version: "1.0.0"
    authors:
      - family-names: Labarrère
        given-names: Mickaël
        alias: mlabarrere
    abstract: >-
      A complete snapshot of the database Idéfix collected (a PostgreSQL 17
      dump): channels and posts of public Telegram channels, comments from
      their public linked discussion groups, including the commenters'
      identifiers, usernames and text, and the derived tables of an earlier
      pipeline run, which scripts/pipeline.py recomputes.
    url: "https://github.com/mlabarrere/Idefix/releases/tag/dataset-v1.0.0"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/mlabarrere/Idefix"
    notes: >-
      Files pinned by SHA-256 in dataset/manifest.json; datasheet and terms of
      use in dataset/DATASHEET.md.
    keywords:
      - telegram
      - dataset
      - public-channels
